<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicolás de Ovando</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1460–1511</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicolás de Ovando was a Spanish knight of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-alcantara">Order of Alcántara</a> and governor of the Indies at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> from 1502 to 1509. He rebuilt Santo Domingo after a hurricane, organised the forced labour of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> and crushed their chiefdoms, notably by the massacre at Jaragua in 1503 and the war against Higüey. His rule made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> the base of Spanish power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicolas-de-ovando.jpg" alt="Nicolás de Ovando" width="319" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicol%C3%A1s_de_Ovando_y_C%C3%A1ceres.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
